{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1788267960,"nonce":"GfYKsWDxK7lEcR3fIfjZxds2F1c=","target":"c718e4a8f3886ce2d1e08cfd5cdea01138bfe75d00d33e1849958c55af87c2db","message":"Session 13 live-bench finding (bench `20260901T121508`), verified against the decompiled 1.6 source. Deterministic, so it lands at the mod rung per DESIGN's 2026-09-01 ruling. Evan's framing of the requirement, 2026-09-01: **\"the agent looks at an area 2-3x bigger than whatever they're building.\"**\n\n\n`find-rect {w:3,h:2,require:[\"buildable\"]}` approved `at:[125,128]` (result `accs13-025-findrect`). `dev:spawn-thing {def:\"HiTechResearchBench\", pos:[125,128], mode:\"direct\"}` then refused: `\"Interaction spot is blocked by granite.\"` (journal seq 38; seq 35/42 the same for `SimpleResearchBench`; `accs13-029` the same one cell over). The agent had asked \"is this box clear\" and been told yes; the thing that refused was outside the box.\n\n\n**1. `find-rect` surveys the footprint and nothing else.** `SpatialVerbs.CheckRect` walks only the rect's own cells: fog, `GetEdifice`, and a hard-coded `TerrainAffordanceDefOf.Heavy`. It takes `w,h`, never a def, so it cannot know that a bench has an interaction cell one cell south of its footprint (`Buildings_Production.xml`: `HiTechResearchBench` `size (5,2)`, `interactionCellOffset (0,0,-1)`, `hasInteractionCell true`; `SimpleResearchBench` `(3,2)`, same offset). The game's gate does know: `GenSpawn.CanSpawnAt` and `GenConstruct.CanPlaceBlueprintAt` both call `GenConstruct.InteractionCellStandable`, which walks `ThingUtility.InteractionCellsWhenAt` and refuses any thing there whose `def.passability != Traversability.Standable` — with the sentence `InteractionSpotBlocked` (`Core/Languages/English/Keyed/Designators.xml`). Granite is Impassable. A chair is NOT refused: `DiningChair` → `ArtableFurnitureBase` → `FurnitureWithQualityBase` → `FurnitureBase` → `BuildingBase` sets no `passability`, and the enum's first value is `Standable`.\n\n**2. `find-rect`'s `at` is a CORNER; the spawn/build verbs take a CENTRE — and for even sizes the game has two centres.** `GenAdj.OccupiedRect(center, rot, size)` is `new CellRect(center.x - (size.x-1)/2, center.z - (size.z-1)/2, ...)`; `CellRect.CenterCell` is `minX + Width/2, minZ + Height/2`. For a 3x2 box with corner (125,128): the game will place a 3x2 def about (126,128) to fill that box, while `find-rect` publishes `center:[126,129]`. The suite passed `at` as `pos`, so the bench landed one cell west of the approved box; passing `center` would have landed it one cell north. **No argument the caller can pass to today's verbs reproduces an even-sized approved rect.** The survey must publish the `pos` the game wants, computed the game's way.\n\n**3. `buildable` is a proxy, not the gate.** Hard-coded `Heavy` where `CanBuildOnTerrain` uses `entDef.GetTerrainAffordanceNeed(stuff)` (`BenchBase` needs `Medium`); no `NotBlockingAnyInteractionCells` (our footprint must not cover a cardinal neighbour's interaction cell); no PlaceWorkers at all — `PlaceWorker_PreventInteractionSpotOverlap.AllowsPlacing` scans the 3x3 around each of OUR interaction cells for any thing (blueprints included, via `entityDefToBuild`) whose own interaction cell is the same cell, and both research benches carry it. `reachable-from:P` tests the rect's centre cell only, not the cell a pawn must stand on to use the thing.\n\n\n- **Footprint** — solid: the cells the thing occupies. `CanPlaceBlueprintAt`'s own walk: bounds, `InNoBuildEdgeArea`, fog, `CanBuildOnTerrain` over the whole rect with the def's real affordance, `CanPlaceBlueprintOver` per occupant (haulable items pass — they get hauled; buildings do not).\n- **Interaction cell(s)** — must be Standable and free of unstandable blueprints/frames (`InteractionCellStandable`); exclusive against OTHER things' interaction cells (`PlaceWorker_PreventInteractionSpotOverlap`); tolerates a chair. Also the reverse: our footprint must not sit on a neighbour's interaction cell (`NotBlockingAnyInteractionCells`).\n- **Margin** — NOT a game gate; computed facts the agent judges with: is the interaction cell reachable from the colony anchor / a named pawn (`map.reachability.CanReach`, `PathEndMode.OnCell`), which cells of the surrounding ring are standable, doors adjacent, and — once `bac4eba` lands — whether the origin is on module phase and the neighbouring module cells are still clear. This tier is where \"2-3x bigger\" lives.\n\n\n**`site-survey {def, pos|at, rot?, stuff?, margin?}`** — a READ. `pos` is the game's centre; `at` is a corner and is converted. Returns:\n- `pos`, `rot`, `footprint` rect (`at`,`w`,`h`) — the exact arguments for `build` (3.3) or `dev:spawn-thing`.\n- `verdict`: the `AcceptanceReport` of `GenConstruct.CanPlaceBlueprintAt(def, pos, rot, map, godMode:false, stuffDef:stuff)` — the game's own sentence, verbatim — plus the widget gate 3.3 owes (`Designator_Build.Visible`: research via `WorldSafe.Finished`, tech level, difficulty, `IsBuildDesignatorVisible`) reported as its own field so \"would be refused\" and \"cannot even be selected\" never read alike.\n- `tiers.footprint[]`, `tiers.interaction[]`, `tiers.margin[]`: per-cell `{at, role, ok, reason, blocker:{def,label,removal,reason}}` in `Blockers.cs`'s shape, so 3.3's preflight and the agent can choose \"clear it\" vs \"site elsewhere\".\n- `view`: an ASCII crop from `CropRenderer` of the footprint expanded by `margin` cells per side (default `max(3, max(w,h))`, so the longer axis is at least 3x; capped at `CropRenderer.MaxSide`), with an overlay layer marking footprint / interaction / margin cells, carrying `CropRenderer.AlphabetId` plus the overlay's own identity so it can be keyed against `map-view` and the PNG channel (`e6faa51`). This is the picture the agent reads mid-loop; it is what would have shown \"the row south of the box is all rock\".\n\n**`find-rect` gains `def` (+`rot`,`stuff`).** When given, `w,h` are forbidden (the def sizes the rect, rotation included via `GenAdj.AdjustForRotation`), each candidate is gated by the same routine `site-survey` uses instead of `CheckRect`, and each candidate publishes `pos` (the game's centre) beside `at`. Without `def`, behaviour is unchanged. `rejected`/`blockers` tally the game's reason strings.\n\n**One shared routine** — `SiteGate` or similar — serves `site-survey`, `find-rect{def}`, `dev:spawn-thing {buildable:true}` and the audit (``3a5ff6c``), and 3.3's `build`/`place-layout` preflight. 3.3 consumes it; it does not re-implement it.\n\n\nThree consumers, three answers, one source of truth. The **structured survey is the contract** — it is what a verb acts on and what a suite proves by shape. The **ASCII crop rides in the same result** because the agent reads it mid-loop with no round trip, in the alphabet `map-view` already uses. The **PNG stays CLI-side**: 2.5's invariant is \"no game-side image rendering; render is a pure function of dump + catalog\", so `rwa render` gains an optional overlay input that is exactly `site-survey`'s tiers — scope note filed on `f7b6207`. No PNG in the mod.\n\n\n`CanPlaceBlueprintAt` is what `Designator_Build` runs under the cursor every frame; `BuildableDef.PlaceWorkers` is a lazy-init getter (instantiates the def's PlaceWorker list on first read) — def-level, never scribed, and the game does the same on the first hover, so it is acceptable and must be recorded in the code comment. Mod PlaceWorkers are third-party code: wrap `AllowsPlacing` in the same try/catch discipline `WhyNoSpawn` uses.\n\n\n- Replay the bench case: `site-survey {def:\"HiTechResearchBench\", at:[125,128]}` on a map staged so the cell south of the footprint is rock. `verdict.reason` is the game's `InteractionSpotBlocked` sentence; `tiers.interaction[0]` names the granite cell with `removal:\"mine\"`; `view` shows the rock row; `pos` is `[127,128]`, and `dev:spawn-thing {pos: \u003cthat\u003e}` after mining it lands with `spawned[0].at == pos` and an occupied rect equal to `footprint`.\n- A chair on the interaction cell: `verdict.ok:true`, the chair listed under `tiers.interaction` as tolerated. A second bench whose interaction cell is the same cell: refused with `InteractionSpotOverlaps`, and the verdict is IDENTICAL to what `build` (3.3) later returns for the same arguments — same routine, proven by the same call.\n- `find-rect {def:\"HiTechResearchBench\"}` returns only candidates the survey accepts; each carries `pos`; `w`/`h` alongside `def` is `bad-args`. `find-rect {w,h}` output is byte-for-byte what it was.\n- Even-size convention: for a `(3,2)` def the published `pos` and `footprint` agree with `GenAdj.OccupiedRect(pos, rot, size)` — asserted by spawning and reading the thing's `OccupiedRect()` back.\n- `margin` default yields a view whose longer side is ≥ 3x the footprint's; `margin:0` yields the footprint plus interaction cells only; the view carries an alphabet identity.\n- Shapes asserted per `accept/` convention (a missing key is a FAIL, not `eq(None)`). Zero red errors.\n\n`1adc737` (3.3 consumes the routine; its instant mode is the F2 issue), `bac4eba` (margin tier's module-phase read), `f7b6207` (PNG overlay input), `e6faa51` (overlay alphabet identity), `acee526` (pos/at convention), ``8b4839f`` (the refusing cell). Evidence: `transcripts/20260901T121508/064-find-rect/cmd.json`, bench `results/accs13-025-findrect.json`, `accs13-026/028/029-devspawnthing.json`, journal `20260901T121508.ndjson` seq 35/38/42.","files":null}]}